{
  "families": [
    {
      "family": "pipelined",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 13, "high": 17, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 16, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["round"]}
      ],
      "budget_share": 50,
      "why": "Pipelined gives the highest Fmax and lowest latency per iteration, making the 32-request burst deadline (sys_p99_batch_us <= 0.44) easiest to meet. We restrict n_iter to 10..16 to keep latency N+2 low enough that 32 results finish within 0.44 us even at moderate Fmax. data_width 13..17 covers the accuracy threshold (W>=14 needed for 2^-12) while allowing area minimisation. angle_guard and frac_guard are kept small to reduce area; round rounding is fixed because trunc is unlikely to meet the error bound at low W."
    },
    {
      "family": "pipelined_m",
      "ranges": [
        {"param": "data_width", "low": 13, "high": 17, "choices": null},
        {"param": "n_iter", "low": 10, "high": 20, "choices": null},
        {"param": "angle_guard", "low": -1, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "frac_guard", "low": 0, "high": 2, "choices": null},
        {"param": "rounding", "low": null, "high": null, "choices": ["round"]},
        {"param": "m", "low": 2, "high": 4, "choices": null}
      ],
      "budget_share": 50,
      "why": "pipelined_m reduces flip-flop count by registering every m stages, directly targeting the min luts_plus_ffs objective. Its latency ceil(N/m)+2 is lower than pipelined for the same N, so we can allow n_iter up to 20 for better accuracy without violating the batch deadline. m=2..4 balances area savings against the longer combinational path (lower Fmax); m>4 risks failing the throughput/batch constraints. Same data_width and guard ranges as pipelined to cover the feasible accuracy region."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The spec requires throughput >= 32 Msps, max_abs_err <= 2^-12, and a 32-request burst to complete within 0.44 us of a 1 MHz tick. Both pipelined and pipelined_m deliver 1 result/cycle, so throughput is satisfied as long as Fmax >= 32 MHz. The critical constraints are accuracy (needs data_width >= 14 and sufficient n_iter) and the burst deadline (needs low latency and high Fmax). Pipelined offers the best Fmax and lowest per-iteration latency, while pipelined_m trades Fmax for fewer FFs, which is attractive for the area objective. We allocate equal budget to both to map the area-accuracy trade-off. Ranges are narrowed around the likely feasible region: data_width 13..17 (W=13 may fail, W=17 gives margin), n_iter 10..16 for pipelined (latency control) and 10..20 for pipelined_m (latency relaxed by m), angle_guard -1..2, frac_guard 0..2, and rounding fixed to round to avoid wasting evaluations on trunc, which is unlikely to meet the error bound at low W. This plan uses the full 100-evaluation budget across two families and four rounds, focusing on the Pareto front between LUTs+FFs and accuracy."
}

{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "Final round: only stop/infeasible are admissible, and the front is clearly feasible, so infeasible is not warranted. All three constraints are met with margin by the 5-design Pareto front: throughput_msps best seen 282 vs required 32 (0% violations), sys_p99_batch_us best 0.154 vs 0.44 (0% violations), and max_abs_err best 0.000109 (2^-13.16) vs the 2^-12 = 0.000244 limit (68% of evaluations violate it, but the front does not). The front spans luts_plus_ffs 1193..2032 against the HV reference 4000 and accuracy_bits 12.5..13.2 against the reference 12, i.e. it already covers the accuracy objective past the reference and the area objective over a wide band, giving hypervolume 3131. The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) is satisfied by pipelined_m [data_width=17 n_iter=15 angle_guard=1 frac_guard=0 rounding=round m=3] at luts_plus_ffs=1193, accuracy_bits=12.5, throughput 124 MSPS, sys_p99_batch 0.154 us — comfortably inside every constraint. The remaining unexplored families (iterative, unrolled_k) are strictly lower-throughput per area on this spec (iterative/unrolled_k give one result every several cycles, while the 32-request burst needs the 1-result/cycle pipelined/pipelined_m behaviour that already dominates the front), so no further gain is expected within the remaining budget. Stopping with the current feasible front."
  ,
  "next_plan": null
}
